<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The Push Notifications capability, task 2.14 of `deliver-push-notifications`.
  Without this entitlement iOS refuses `registerForRemoteNotifications()`
  outright, so every function in `src/lib/push/registration.ts` resolves and no
  token ever arrives.

  `$(APS_ENVIRONMENT)` is a build setting, defined per configuration in
  `project.pbxproj` — `development` for Debug, `production` for Release. Xcode
  expands build variables in an entitlements file at the `ProcessProductPackaging`
  step, the same mechanism `$(AppIdentifierPrefix)` uses. A hardcoded value would
  match automatic signing in one configuration and fail to sign in the other;
  hardcoding `development` in particular ships a TestFlight build that registers
  against the sandbox and receives nothing from production APNs.

  `docs/reference/native-shell.md` §Push registration is provisioned in the
  project has the rest, including why no `remote-notification` background mode
  is declared here.
-->
<!--
  The Associated Domains capability, PD-205. Without this entitlement iOS never
  fetches `https://app.letsride.social/.well-known/apple-app-site-association`,
  so the signup confirmation link, a shared ride and a shared postcard all open
  Safari and leave the installed app where it was.

  **Those three, and NOT password recovery — iOS does not hand off on a
  redirect.** A universal link fires only for a tap on a URL whose host is the
  associated domain; a 302 that arrives at that host does not count.
  `supabase/templates/confirm-signup.html` uses
  `{{ .SiteURL }}/auth/confirm?token_hash=…`, a direct `app.letsride.social`
  URL, which is why confirmation works. `reset-password.html` still uses
  `{{ .ConfirmationURL }}`, which is a `…supabase.co/auth/v1/verify` link that
  redirects to our host — so recovery keeps opening the browser until that
  template is changed, and no entitlement here can alter it.

  `applinks:` and nothing else. The other prefixes this key accepts are for
  capabilities this app does not have: `webcredentials:` is shared-password
  autofill and `activitycontinuation:` is Handoff, and each would claim a
  capability that has to be enabled on the App ID and tested on a device.

  **Production only, deliberately.** `app-dev.letsride.social` sits behind
  Vercel SSO (`docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md` §Domains), and Apple's CDN fetches the
  association file with no credential — so a DEV entry could never verify, and
  listing one would produce a build whose universal links silently fall back to
  the browser and read as a broken implementation rather than an unverifiable
  host. The native bundle is built against `https://app.letsride.social` in any
  case (`next.config.ts`'s `NEXT_PUBLIC_CANONICAL_ORIGIN` guard), so there is no
  bundle for which a DEV entry would be the right one.

  **Two things outside this repository have to be true**, and neither can be
  checked here: Associated Domains must be enabled on the App ID in the Apple
  Developer portal so the provisioning profile carries it, and the file above
  must be served over HTTPS with no redirect and no auth. `docs/reference/native-shell.md`
  §Universal links has both, and the first device test is the only thing that
  proves either.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>$(APS_ENVIRONMENT)</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:app.letsride.social</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
